                <studyAreaDescription>
                    <descriptor name="generic" citableClassificationSystem="false">
                        <descriptorValue>Arabuko Sokoke Forest (ASF) is the largest area of coastal forest remaining in East Africa and a major Important Bird Area in mainland Kenya. Arabuko Sokoke Forest (ASF), with a total area of approximately 41 600 ha, is the largest surviving single block of the previously extensive indigenous coastal tropical forest in Eastern Africa.</descriptorValue>
